@startuml update-tracking
!include _theme.puml

title Two ways to follow gisnix — your flake.nix decides

rectangle "Your machine's **flake.nix**\n(the gisnix input line)" as flake #F5F5F2

rectangle "**Pinned to a version**\n`url = \"github:kartoza/gisnix/v0.19.0\"`" as pin
rectangle "**Tracking main**\n`url = \"github:kartoza/gisnix\"`" as main

flake --> pin
flake --> main

note bottom of pin
  A tag never moves, so `nix flake update`
  changes nothing until **you** edit the
  version. You decide when to step forward.
  Reproducible and calm — the safer choice.
end note

note bottom of main
  main moves with every commit, so
  `nix flake update` jumps to the newest
  gisnix — released or not. Newest features,
  the occasional rough edge. For the bold.
end note

@enduml
